"""Frozen-source entropy certificate repair for the Gate C exact ray.

Audit response (2026-08-31, Main five-point audit; STATIC ONLY, no compute):
  1. Loads the three checksummed campaign `.asrun` dependencies via explicit
     importlib/sys.modules injection (AI: AUX_LOADER); asserts their SHA-256
     against `checksums.sha256` before importing anything else.
  2. Exact-rational near-dual primal: affine projection onto an exact
     independent row set of B (per-branch, nonnegativity guarded by
     projection-failure detection), full-row/normalization/nonnegativity
     checks with Fractions, entropy lower bound only via Arb on a certified
     feasible point.  An infeasible-overlap plant records that the old
     interval-inclusion test accepts dist_max vectors the exact Fraction test
     rejects.  fallback H(p) when projection fails.
  3. Part/GlobalStage lagrange_constraints -> []).  ceq then retains the two
     structural ret_comp rows + global part (never zeroed).
  4. Repaired penalty fields (installed on gm.dist/G via G-wrapping) are
     written into Part.evaluate_post / GlobalStage.evaluate_post wrapped
     copies so Workspace.c_viol hashing constraints and the manual R loop
     consume the IDENTICAL Ival intervals.  Per-point hash-certificate
     count + key signature asserted (no double counting).
  5. Mandatory bad-multiplier plant is KKT-only (+1/8 dyadic written to a
     Fractions record; a second strictly-worse diagnostic upper bound is
     logged but not required).

Every decision-relevant number remains an Arb interval computed on exact
binary64-dyadic points; solver successes stay COMPUTATIONAL-EVIDENCE.
"""
